      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/raspberries/voice/voice-v4-blocks/09-cons.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "10-closing_summary",
      "index": 9,
      "kind": "closing_summary",
      "sectionKey": null,
      "text": "Big strengths are fibre, vitamin C, and anthocyanin-rich berry pigments, but the biggest weaknesses are low potassium, low vitamin A, and low protein amount. It's good for heart health, digestion, and low-calorie flavour swaps because fibre is useful for heart health, fibre helps digestion and keeps meals steadier, and it adds flavour without adding many calories.",
